\":\"671cf0859791c54c2a6efc22d4db96d4aef3fa700474c47bff6a4e0fe1e14bea\",\"declaration_text\":\"Run one pixel-art command on a drawing or image you already made. This is\\nthe engine's own command line: it checks work, explains it and improves it.\\n\\nCommands: check and explain (read-only):\\n- lint <id> [--rules outline_gap,orphan_pixel,…] — pixel-art defects, each\\n  naming the node and command that drew them\\n- inspect <id> --region x0,y0,x1,y1 --scale 10 — a zoomed crop with its\\n  exact colours\\n- measure <id> --at x,y — what is at a pixel and who drew it\\n- explain <id> — resolved geometry, per-command footprints, before rendering\\n- motion / storyboard / silhouette / reveal / clusters / parts <id> — reports\\n- score <id> — a 0-100 pixel-art discipline score with a breakdown\\n- compare <id> <id> — two results side by side\\nImprove (returns a NEW drawing id):\\n- shade <id> --band 2 --light=-1,-1 — banded shading along a colour ramp\\n- selout <id> — selective outlining; reoutline / clean-lines / aa / mirror\\n- cluster <id> --at x,y --action recolor --color <name> — one guarded cluster\\n- repair <id> — deterministic cleanup of drift, strays, fringe and noise\\nSheets and frames (returns a NEW image id):\\n- split <image> --grid 3x3 — a sprite sheet, strip or grid as an animation,\\n  one frame per cell (columns x rows)\\n- join <image> <image> … [--as sheet|rows|animation] [--columns n] — pictures\\n  or animations as one sprite sheet, one per row, or one animation\\n- scale <image> --by 4 — the same picture or animation bigger, each pixel a\\n  4x4 block (a sticker, a print); nothing is redrawn\\nA result comes back as an image in the reply AND as a no-auth URL the reply\\nprints, `/mcp/pixel-tools/<id>/image.png` (`frames.png` for the frames of a\\nmulti-frame one) — so a sheet you joined is both readable inline and\\ndownloadable. Sheets hold at most 1024 px a side; `join` refuses a larger\\none rather than shrinking the art, and says how many frames do fit.\\nCraft operations need colour ramps: run `extract-palette <id>` first, then\\npass `--ramps skin=dark,mid,light`.\\nAuthoring: `edit <id> --changes '[…]'` applies exact pixel operations and\\n`draw <id> --recipe '{…}'` builds or revises a layered scene; both take JSON\\nwhose fields are NOT listed here. Colours in that JSON are always `#RRGGBB`\\nor `#RRGGBBAA` with alpha `00` or `ff` — `rgb()` and bare hex are refused,\\nand nothing strips the `#`, since argv is a JSON list rather than a shell\\nline. Every `edit` change carries `operation`, `layer`, `frames` (ONE-based)\\nand `reason`; coordinates are zero-based and a `region` is `[x0,y0,x1,y1]`\\ninclusive. Then its own fields: `patch_pixels` takes `pixels`, a list of\\n`[x,y,expected,replacement]` (1-10000, each assigned only where the pixel\\nalready holds `expected`, so a mismatch fails the pass); `copy_region` takes\\n`source_layer`, `source_frame`, `region`, `at` `[x,y]`; `map_colors` takes\\n`region` and `colors` `{\\\"#from\\\":\\\"#to\\\"}` (alpha must match); `flood_fill`\\n`seed`/`expected`/`color`; `brush` `points` plus `color`; `outline` `mode`\\n(outside|inside|recolor|erase). The full contracts and any command's flags\\nare one free call away: `describe edits | paint | outline | draw | animation\\n| motion | scenes | review`, `<command> -h`, `describe cli`.\\nFree for subscribers.\\n\\nPixelLab AI-powered pixel art generation service.\\n\\nUse of this service is subject to PixelLab's Terms of Service:\\nhttps://pixellab.ai/termsofservice\\n\\nThis MCP server provides programmatic access to generate:\\n- Characters with multiple directional views\\n- Character animations\\n- Isometric tiles\\n- Top-down tilesets for game maps\\n- Sidescroller tilesets for platformer games\\n\\nAll generation operations are non-blocking and return job IDs for status tracking.\\nRequires PixelLab subscription (with credit fallback support).\\n\\n**Pixel tools (free, exact, you are the artist)**: one command line, pixelart_workbench(argv=[...]), inspects, edits, draws and animates pixel art by your own decisions; combine it with the AI tools above. Start with pixelart_workbench(argv=['describe', 'start'], mode='low'|'high') — low acts directly with few tokens, high plans out loud and reviews every frame. Animated effects (spells, hits, explosions, auras): vfx_workbench(argv=['describe', 'start']) — same ids, exports to the user's My effects.\\n\\n**Git access**: Clone and push game project source code with standard git.\\nUse `list_projects` to see your projects and their git clone URLs.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__pixellab__pixelart_workbench(args: {\\n  // One command line, e.g. 'lint <drawing_id> --rules outline_gap' or ['edit', '<id>', '--changes', '[…]']. Omit it for the playbook. A subject is an id or an image reference — never a file path; the server writes the output and returns a new id. A reference is `character:<id>:<direction>` for a rotation, `character:<id>:<direction>:<animation>` for every frame of that animation (the display name, type or [group: ...] id get_character prints), the same two forms for `object:<id>` (a one-direction object's direction is the literal `unknown`), `gallery:<id>`, `job:<id>`, `upload:<id>`, a data URL, an https link or base64. That is how a stored animation's pixels come back inline without downloading anything. Start with 'describe cli' for the full command list.\\n  argv?: string | Array<string> | null;\\n  // low (default): act directly, fewest tokens — one decisive image per result. high: think openly — fuller evidence and a review checklist; write your plan and observations in `notes`. Use the mode the user asked for.\\n  mode?: \\\"low\\\" | \\\"high\\\";\\n  // What you observed and what this step should achieve, in a few sentences (high mode: always; low: optional). On the first call, include the user's request. Stored with the step to improve these tools.\\n  notes?: string | null;\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\",\"official_docs\":[\"https://api.pixellab.ai/mcp/docs\",\"https://www.pixellab.ai/docs\"],\"schema_representation\":\"JSON Schema projection of the exposed TypeScript argument declaration: argv string | string[] | null, mode 'low' | 'high', notes string | null; additionalProperties false\",\"subject_transport\":\"Each argv subject is a data:image/png;base64 URL of the exact retained seed bytes (declaration: a subject is an id or an image reference, including a data URL, an https link or base64; never a file path). Base64 computed from the artifact file and verified to round-trip to the same sha256.\"},\"observed_at\":\"2026-11-09T08:31:55+00:00\",\"source\":\"Current connected official PixelLab MCP tool declaration retained in official-discovery.json (host-exposed declaration text; not a raw tools/list dump)\"},\"stale\":[],\"blockers\":[],\"candidates\":[]}],\"pending_jobs\":[],\"next_action\":\"delivered\",\"continuation\":{\"store\":\".pixl/assets/queue.ready\",\"state_hash\":\"88d77c62b47eb8fef5d35015973f67b0f38731cb04e54430efa36aec4b898d64\",\"asset_id\":\"queue.working\",\"requirements_hash\":\"ec61d688f752ac1280914d22ba75bdb4e8f7e31c42b18d7d62f7a14038eedea5\",\"task\":\"artistic-02.working.task\",\"action\":\"delivered\",\"delivery\":{\"destination\":\"assets/working.png\",\"candidate\":\"artistic2.working.candidate\",\"expected_sha256\":\"cf101610108f5a708987dfeb1a86ae9921525464d24c19953a889e20603176dc\",\"observed_sha256\":\"cf101610108f5a708987dfeb1a86ae9921525464d24c19953a889e20603176dc\",\"destination_matches\":true,\"families\":[{\"output\":\"artistic-02.delivery.output\",\"task\":\"artistic-02.delivery.task\",\"state\":\"done\",\"candidate\":\"artistic2.delivery.candidate\",\"accepted\":true,\"member_selection_current\":true,\"manifest\":\".pixl/assets/queue.ready/deliveries/1060114444f6c41150cb3914098f920790b29d47458af5c3ab33c43910b3c211/manifest.json\",\"manifest_sha256\":\"1060114444f6c41150cb3914098f92